cvc5's process dies immediately on the preceding command's fatal error, before ever reaching the follow-up command that checks whether the failed :named symbol leaked -- that check is fundamentally unobservable for cvc5 (not just flaky), and the exact cascade tail on the way there is itself a race between jSMTLIB's main loop and the OS noticing the broken pipe (differs between in-process JUnit and subprocess shell execution).
